# Working with BLoC

- **No UI concerns in BLoCs** — no `BuildContext`, toasts, dialogs or
  navigation inside a BLoC/Cubit. Emit pure immutable state; the UI reacts
  with `BlocListener` / `BlocBuilder`.
- **BLoCs talk through events**, not direct service/method calls
  (`audioBloc.add(PlayTapAudio())`, not `audioService.playTap()`). The one
  documented exception: `SettingBloc.audioBloc` is set so `ToggleMute` can
  reach the active `AudioBloc` (`lib/navs/menu_nav.dart`).
- **State is immutable** — change it only through `copyWith` + `emit`. Add a
  `copyWith` parameter for every new field (see `TutorialState`).
- **Navigation is cubit-driven**: `PlayerNavCubit` / `CombatNavCubit` states
  decide the `pages:` of the nested `Navigator`s in `lib/navs/`. Navigate by
  calling the cubit (`showPlay()`, `showPlaying()`), never `Navigator.push`.
- **`TutorialCubit` holds no bloc references** (`TurnBloc`/`CombatBloc` only
  exist inside the Play branch and `CombatBloc` is recreated per match). Host
  screens observe it and seed / navigate themselves; see
  `onboarding-tour.mdc`.
- **Timer pausing uses holds**: add / release a `TimerPauseReason`
  (`TapTimerPause` / `TapTimerResume`) instead of toggling a bool, so the
  in-game menu, the app lifecycle, layout changes and the combat opponent
  can't unpause each other (`lib/blocs/objects/timer_pause.dart`).
- Infrastructure blocs (`TourBloc`, `MenuBloc`, `SettingBloc`, `AudioBloc`,
  `VibrationBloc`) come from `skeleton_core`; `lib/blocs/objects/tour/` only
  re-exports `TourBloc`/`TourState`.
